-- Spin-1/2 Dominance Theorem for Black-Hole Entropy:
-- Comparing a single puncture of doubled spin d (area-squared ∝ d(d+2), Hilbert dim d+1)
-- against d spin-1/2 punctures (total area-squared ∝ 3d, Hilbert dim 2^d):
-- For every d ≥ 2 (every higher spin j ≥ 1), replacing one spin-d/2 puncture with d spin-1/2
-- punctures yields STRICTLY LESS area (3d < d(d+2)) AND STRICTLY MORE microstates (d+1 < 2^d),
-- proving why Bekenstein–Hawking entropy is overwhelmingly dominated by j = 1/2 punctures.
lqg-pow2 : Nat → Nat
lqg-pow2 n = case n of
  zero → 1
  suc k → plus (lqg-pow2 k) (lqg-pow2 k)
